IMPORT prelude

-- Statutory Declarations Act 1959 (Commonwealth) -- how may I make a Commonwealth statutory declaration, who may witness
-- it, what may it be used for, and what happens if what I declare is false?
--
-- SEAT: the declarant, and the person asked to witness the declaration. Every decision is phrased as one of them asks it,
-- from facts they could state. Where the Act speaks to someone else (the provider of an online platform, s 9B; the courts,
-- s 12), the encoding says what it means for the declarant.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 4 ("declarant", "prescribed person", "video link", "approved online platform", "approved identity
-- service"), s 5 (where the Act applies), s 6 (anyone may declare; what a declaration may be used for), s 7A (signing by
-- hand or electronically), s 8 (the two ways a declaration is made), s 9 (observation by a prescribed person, in person or
-- by video link), s 9A (digital verification on an approved online platform), s 9B(1) (the platform must not keep a copy),
-- s 10 (a declaration another Commonwealth law requires to be made before someone), s 11 (false statements; 4 years), s 13
-- with Endnote 5 (the external Territories the Act reaches).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 8, compilation date 1 January 2024 ("Includes amendments: Act No. 92, 2023"; register id
-- C2024C00005), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1959A00052.txt (retrieved 2026-10-13).
-- Instruments: the Statutory Declarations Regulations 2023 are NOT deposited. Everything they settle is an INPUT: who is a
-- prescribed person (s 4; Schedule 1 of the Regulations), which digital service is an approved online platform (s 9A(2))
-- or an approved identity service (s 9A(3)), the identity-verification conditions (s 9A(1)(b)(ii)) and the platform
-- information a digital declaration must carry (s 9A(1)(c)(ii)). The approved forms (s 15) are not deposited either; whether
-- a declaration is "in the approved form" is an input. The Act does not name myGov or any other platform.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the saving of 1911-Act declarations (s 3); the meaning of "Magistrate", "State" and "Territory" beyond the
-- s 5 question; references in other laws (s 7) beyond s 10; the provider's annual report (s 9B(2)-(5)); the jurisdiction
-- of courts and procedure (s 12); regulation-making and the Minister's preconditions (s 14); approval of forms (s 15); the
-- review (s 16). Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code (applied by s 5A) is not deposited: the fault element for the falsity of the
-- statement is an INPUT, and the conversion of the 4-year term into a fine (Crimes Act 1914) is not encoded.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use as advice.

§ `Statutory Declarations Act 1959`

§§ `5 and 13 -- does the Act reach the place where I make my declaration`

-- s 5(1): "Subject to this section, this Act applies both within and without the Commonwealth."
-- s 5(2): "Except as provided by subsection 12(8), this Act does not apply in a Territory not forming part of the
-- Commonwealth unless this Act extends to that Territory by virtue of section 13."
-- s 13: "this Act extends to Norfolk Island and to such other Territories not forming part of the Commonwealth as the
-- Governor-General, by Proclamation, declares." Endnote 5 records Proclamations for Christmas Island and the Cocos
-- (Keeling) Islands (1972) and for the Australian Antarctic Territory, the Coral Sea Islands Territory, Ashmore and Cartier
-- Islands, and Heard Island and McDonald Islands (1993).
-- "Territory not forming part of the Commonwealth" is the Act's phrase; which places are such Territories is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Place` IS ONE OF
    `in a State or a Territory forming part of the Commonwealth`
    `in a foreign country`
    `in Norfolk Island`
    `in an external Territory named in a Proclamation under s 13`
    `in another Territory not forming part of the Commonwealth`

@export Does the Statutory Declarations Act apply where I make my declaration (ss 5, 13)?
GIVEN `where I am` IS A `Place` @desc Where you are when you make the declaration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act apply where I make my declaration` IF
    CONSIDER `where I am`
    WHEN `in another Territory not forming part of the Commonwealth` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `6 -- what my declaration may be used for`

-- s 6(1): "A person may, if the person so desires, make a statutory declaration in relation to any matter."
-- s 6(2): "Subject to subsection (3), a statutory declaration may be used: (a) for the purposes of a law of the
-- Commonwealth or of a Territory, unless the contrary intention appears in that law; (b) in connection with any matter
-- arising under a law of the Commonwealth or of a Territory, unless the contrary intention appears in that law; or (c) in
-- connection with the administration of any Department of State of the Commonwealth."
-- s 6(3): "Subsection (2) does not authorise a statutory declaration to be used as evidence in a judicial proceeding but
-- nothing in this section prevents a statutory declaration from being so used."
DECLARE `Use` IS ONE OF
    `for the purposes of a Commonwealth or Territory law`
    `in connection with a matter arising under a Commonwealth or Territory law`
    `in connection with the administration of a Commonwealth Department of State`
    `as evidence in a judicial proceeding`
    `for some other purpose, such as a State law or a private matter`

DECLARE `What s 6 says about my use` IS ONE OF
    `s 6(2) authorises this use`
    `not authorised: the law shows a contrary intention`
    `not authorised by s 6(2), but s 6 does not prevent its use as evidence`
    `not authorised by s 6(2): this Act neither authorises nor forbids it`

@export May I make a statutory declaration about any matter I choose (s 6(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make a statutory declaration about any matter` IS TRUE

@export May my Commonwealth statutory declaration be used for this purpose (s 6(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the use` IS A `Use` @desc What the declaration is to be used for
      `the law shows a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commonwealth or Territory law concerned shows an intention that a statutory declaration under this Act is not to be used
GIVETH A `What s 6 says about my use`
DECIDE `May my declaration be used for this` IS
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `for the purposes of a Commonwealth or Territory law` THEN
        IF `the law shows a contrary intention` THEN `not authorised: the law shows a contrary intention` ELSE `s 6(2) authorises this use`
    WHEN `in connection with a matter arising under a Commonwealth or Territory law` THEN
        IF `the law shows a contrary intention` THEN `not authorised: the law shows a contrary intention` ELSE `s 6(2) authorises this use`
    WHEN `in connection with the administration of a Commonwealth Department of State` THEN `s 6(2) authorises this use`
    WHEN `as evidence in a judicial proceeding` THEN `not authorised by s 6(2), but s 6 does not prevent its use as evidence`
    OTHERWISE `not authorised by s 6(2): this Act neither authorises nor forbids it`

§§ `7A -- signing by hand or electronically`

-- s 7A(1): "a person may sign a statutory declaration by signing: (a) a physical form of the declaration by hand; or (b) an
-- electronic form of the declaration using electronic means; if the method of signing satisfies subsection (2)."
-- s 7A(2): "(a) the method identifies the person and indicates the person's intention in respect of the information
-- recorded in the declaration; and (b) the method was either: (i) as reliable as appropriate for the purpose for which the
-- information was recorded, in light of all the circumstances, including any relevant agreement; or (ii) proven in fact to
-- have fulfilled the functions described in paragraph (a), by itself or together with further evidence."
-- s 7A is permissive ("may sign"); it does not say that any other method fails. The encoding answers only whether s 7A
-- recognises the method.
DECLARE `Signing` IS ONE OF
    `by hand on a physical form`
    `by electronic means on an electronic form`
    `some other way`

@export Does s 7A recognise the way I signed my statutory declaration?
GIVEN `how I signed` IS A `Signing` @desc How you signed the declaration
      `the method identifies me and shows my intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the method identifies you and shows your intention about the information in the declaration
      `the method was reliable enough or proven in fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the method was as reliable as appropriate for the purpose, or was proven in fact to identify you and show your intention
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does s 7A recognise my signature` IF
        (CONSIDER `how I signed`
         WHEN `some other way` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND `the method identifies me and shows my intention`
    AND `the method was reliable enough or proven in fact`

§§ `8, 9, 9A -- is my declaration made under the Act`

-- s 8: "A statutory declaration made under this Act must satisfy the requirements of either: (a) section 9 (observation by
-- prescribed person); or (b) section 9A (digital verification)."
-- s 4: "prescribed person means a person prescribed by the regulations to be a prescribed person." The Regulations are not
-- deposited: whether the witness is one is an INPUT.
-- s 4: "video link means facilities that enable audio and visual communication between persons in different places."
DECLARE `Way of making` IS ONE OF
    `signed while a witness watched in person`
    `signed while a witness watched by video link`
    `completed and signed on an online platform`
    `signed with no witness watching and no online platform`

DECLARE `Declaration` HAS
    `in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the declaration is in a form the Minister approved under s 15
    `how I signed` IS A `Signing`
    `my signing method identifies me and shows my intention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my signing method was reliable enough or proven in fact` IS A BOOLEAN
    `how it was made` IS A `Way of making`
    `the witness is a prescribed person` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the witness is prescribed by the Statutory Declarations Regulations 2023 (not deposited)
    `the witness signed the declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the witness signed a copy they were satisfied is a true copy` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc After a video link: whether the witness signed a copy they were satisfied is a true copy of what you signed
    `the platform is an approved online platform` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the digital service is prescribed by the Regulations as an approved online platform (not deposited)
    `my identity was verified by an approved identity service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the verification met the prescribed conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it carries the prescribed platform information` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it includes information provided by the platform of a kind the Regulations prescribe

DECLARE `How my declaration stands` IS ONE OF
    `made under s 9: signed under a prescribed person's observation in person`
    `made under s 9: signed under a prescribed person's observation by video link`
    `made under s 9A: digitally verified on an approved online platform`
    `not made under the Act: not in the approved form`
    `not made under the Act: not signed in a way s 7A recognises`
    `not made under the Act: no witness watched and no online platform was used`
    `not made under the Act: the witness is not a prescribed person`
    `not made under the Act: the witness signed neither the declaration nor, after a video link, a true copy`
    `not made under the Act: the platform is not an approved online platform`
    `not made under the Act: my identity was not verified as s 9A(1)(b) requires`
    `not made under the Act: it lacks the platform information s 9A(1)(c) requires`

-- s 9: "(a) the declaration is in the approved form; and (b) the declaration is signed by the declarant under the
-- observation of a prescribed person in either of the following cases: (i) in person; (ii) by video link; and (c) either:
-- (i) in any case--the declaration is signed by the prescribed person; or (ii) in the case where the prescribed person
-- observes the declarant sign the declaration by video link and is satisfied that a copy of the declaration is a true copy
-- of the declaration signed by the declarant (whether or not the copy includes the declarant's signature)--that copy is
-- signed by the prescribed person."
GIVEN `d` IS A `Declaration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `watched by video link` IF
    CONSIDER `d`'s `how it was made`
    WHEN `signed while a witness watched by video link` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `d` IS A `Declaration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `signed as s 7A recognises` IF
    `Does s 7A recognise my signature` (`d`'s `how I signed`)
        (`d`'s `my signing method identifies me and shows my intention`)
        (`d`'s `my signing method was reliable enough or proven in fact`)

GIVEN `d` IS A `Declaration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the witness signed what s 9(c) requires` IF
        `d`'s `the witness signed the declaration`
    OR  (`watched by video link` `d` AND `d`'s `the witness signed a copy they were satisfied is a true copy`)

GIVEN `d` IS A `Declaration`
GIVETH A `How my declaration stands`
DECIDE `the s 9 outcome` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `d`'s `the witness is a prescribed person`)
            THEN `not made under the Act: the witness is not a prescribed person`
        IF (NOT `the witness signed what s 9(c) requires` `d`)
            THEN `not made under the Act: the witness signed neither the declaration nor, after a video link, a true copy`
        IF `watched by video link` `d`
            THEN `made under s 9: signed under a prescribed person's observation by video link`
        OTHERWISE `made under s 9: signed under a prescribed person's observation in person`

-- s 9A(1): "(a) the declaration: (i) is in the approved form; and (ii) is completed and signed by the declarant using an
-- approved online platform; and (b) the identity of the declarant is verified: (i) using an approved identity service; and
-- (ii) in accordance with the conditions prescribed by the regulations; and (c) the declaration includes information that:
-- (i) is provided by the approved online platform; and (ii) is of a kind prescribed by the regulations."
-- s 9A(2): "An approved online platform is a digital service that is prescribed by the regulations to be an approved online
-- platform." s 9A(3) is the same for an approved identity service. The Act names no platform: whether myGov (or any other
-- service) is one is an INPUT.
GIVEN `d` IS A `Declaration`
GIVETH A `How my declaration stands`
DECIDE `the s 9A outcome` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `d`'s `the platform is an approved online platform`)
            THEN `not made under the Act: the platform is not an approved online platform`
        IF (NOT `d`'s `my identity was verified by an approved identity service`) OR (NOT `d`'s `the verification met the prescribed conditions`)
            THEN `not made under the Act: my identity was not verified as s 9A(1)(b) requires`
        IF (NOT `d`'s `it carries the prescribed platform information`)
            THEN `not made under the Act: it lacks the platform information s 9A(1)(c) requires`
        OTHERWISE `made under s 9A: digitally verified on an approved online platform`

-- Both routes need the approved form (s 9(a), s 9A(1)(a)(i)) and a signature (s 9(b), s 9A(1)(a)(ii)), which s 7A says how
-- to give. The limbs are checked in the order the text gives them; the first that fails is reported.
@export Is my statutory declaration made under the Act, and by which route (ss 8, 9, 9A)?
GIVEN `my declaration` IS A `Declaration` @desc How your declaration was prepared, signed and witnessed or verified
GIVETH A `How my declaration stands`
DECIDE `Is my declaration made under the Act` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `my declaration`'s `in the approved form`)
            THEN `not made under the Act: not in the approved form`
        IF (NOT `signed as s 7A recognises` `my declaration`)
            THEN `not made under the Act: not signed in a way s 7A recognises`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `my declaration`'s `how it was made`
            WHEN `signed while a witness watched in person` THEN `the s 9 outcome` `my declaration`
            WHEN `signed while a witness watched by video link` THEN `the s 9 outcome` `my declaration`
            WHEN `completed and signed on an online platform` THEN `the s 9A outcome` `my declaration`
            OTHERWISE `not made under the Act: no witness watched and no online platform was used`

§§ `9 -- the person asked to witness`

-- s 9(b) and (c), from the witness's seat: the witness must be a prescribed person, must observe the declarant sign (in
-- person or by video link), and must sign the declaration -- or, after a video link, a copy they are satisfied is a true
-- copy, "whether or not the copy includes the declarant's signature".
DECLARE `How I observe` IS ONE OF
    `I watch the declarant sign in person`
    `I watch the declarant sign by video link`
    `I do not watch the declarant sign`

DECLARE `What I must sign` IS ONE OF
    `the declaration itself`
    `the declaration itself, or a copy I am satisfied is a true copy, with or without the declarant's signature`
    `nothing: I am not a prescribed person, so I cannot witness under s 9`
    `nothing: s 9 needs me to watch the declarant sign`

@export May I witness this Commonwealth statutory declaration (s 9)?
GIVEN `I am a prescribed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are prescribed by the Statutory Declarations Regulations 2023 (for example by your occupation; the Regulations are not deposited)
      `how I observe` IS A `How I observe` @desc Whether you watch the declarant sign, in person or by video link
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I witness this declaration` IF
        `I am a prescribed person`
    AND (CONSIDER `how I observe`
         WHEN `I do not watch the declarant sign` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

@export As the witness, what must I sign (s 9(c))?
GIVEN `I am a prescribed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are prescribed by the Statutory Declarations Regulations 2023 (not deposited)
      `how I observe` IS A `How I observe` @desc Whether you watch the declarant sign, in person or by video link
GIVETH A `What I must sign`
DECIDE `What must I sign as the witness` IS
    IF (NOT `I am a prescribed person`) THEN `nothing: I am not a prescribed person, so I cannot witness under s 9`
    ELSE
            CONSIDER `how I observe`
            WHEN `I watch the declarant sign in person` THEN `the declaration itself`
            WHEN `I watch the declarant sign by video link` THEN `the declaration itself, or a copy I am satisfied is a true copy, with or without the declarant's signature`
            OTHERWISE `nothing: s 9 needs me to watch the declarant sign`

§§ `9B(1) -- my copy and the platform`

-- s 9B(1): "The provider of an approved online platform must not retain any copy of a statutory declaration that is made
-- using the online platform." For the declarant: the provider may not keep a copy of mine. (No penalty is stated in s 9B;
-- s 14(5) lets the Governor-General repeal the platform's prescription.)
@export May the provider of the approved online platform keep a copy of my declaration (s 9B(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the platform keep a copy of my declaration` IS FALSE

§§ `10 -- a declaration another Commonwealth law says is made before someone`

-- s 10: "Where, by a law of the Commonwealth or of a Territory ..., a declaration is required to be made by a person before
-- some other person, the declaration may, unless the contrary intention appears in that law, be made before the person
-- mentioned in that law or under the observation of a prescribed person in accordance with section 9."
DECLARE `Before whom` IS ONE OF
    `before the person that law names, or under a prescribed person's observation under s 9`
    `only before the person that law names: it shows a contrary intention`

@export Another Commonwealth law says my declaration is to be made before a particular person: before whom may I make it (s 10)?
GIVEN `that law shows a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that law shows an intention that only the person it names will do
GIVETH A `Before whom`
DECIDE `Before whom may I make the declaration that law requires` IS
    IF `that law shows a contrary intention`
    THEN `only before the person that law names: it shows a contrary intention`
    ELSE `before the person that law names, or under a prescribed person's observation under s 9`

§§ `11 -- a false declaration`

-- s 11: "A person must not intentionally make a false statement in a statutory declaration. Penalty: Imprisonment for 4
-- years."
-- s 5A: "Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code applies to all offences against this Act." Chapter 2 is not deposited. What fault
-- element attaches to the falsity of the statement is settled there, so it is an INPUT, as is whether a defence in
-- Chapter 2 applies.
@export Do I commit the s 11 offence of making a false statement in a statutory declaration?
GIVEN `it is a statutory declaration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document you made is a statutory declaration
      `the statement is false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the statement you made in it is false
      `I made the statement intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you meant to make that statement
      `the fault element for its falsity is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fault element Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code requires as to the falsity is met (for example, you knew it was false)
      `a Criminal Code defence applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a defence under Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code applies to you (for example, mistake of fact)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit the false declaration offence` IF
        `it is a statutory declaration`
    AND `the statement is false`
    AND `I made the statement intentionally`
    AND `the fault element for its falsity is met`
    AND (NOT `a Criminal Code defence applies`)

@export What is the longest I can be imprisoned for a false statement in a statutory declaration (s 11), in years?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for a false declaration in years` IS 4
